<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Patan Durbar Square</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Patan Durbar Square is the old royal square of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lalitpur">Lalitpur</a> (Patan) in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu-valley">Kathmandu Valley</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nepal">Nepal</a>, in front of the palace of the Malla kings of Lalitpur. Most of its temples and palace courtyards date from the 17th and 18th centuries, among them the stone <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/krishna">Krishna</a> Mandir, and the palace now houses the Patan Museum. It is part of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kathmandu">Kathmandu</a> Valley World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/patan-durbar-square.jpg" alt="Patan Durbar Square" width="320" height="232" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Zulufive · CC0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Patan_durbar_square.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
